# EmotionSense — AI Emotion Detection System

A multimodal emotion detection web app that analyzes emotions from **face images**, **voice recordings**, and **text** using deep learning models.

## Features
- Face emotion detection via DeepFace
- Voice emotion detection via CNN trained on RAVDESS dataset
- Text emotion detection via `j-hartmann/emotion-english-distilroberta-base`
- Fusion engine combining all three modalities
- Support suggestions based on detected emotion
- Light/Dark theme toggle

## Tech Stack
- **Backend:** Python, Flask
- **Face:** DeepFace, OpenCV
- **Voice:** TensorFlow/Keras CNN, Librosa
- **Text:** HuggingFace Transformers (RoBERTa)
- **Frontend:** HTML, CSS, Vanilla JS

## Setup

### 1. Clone the repo
```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/face_emotion.git
cd face_emotion
```

### 2. Install dependencies
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 3. Train the voice model (first time only)
```bash
python train_voice_model.py
```
This downloads the RAVDESS dataset (~400MB) and trains the voice emotion model. Saves to `models/voice_model.h5`.

### 4. Run the app
```bash
python app.py
```
Open `http://127.0.0.1:8003` in your browser.

## Notes
- `models/` folder is not included in the repo (too large). Run `train_voice_model.py` to generate it.
- Requires `ffmpeg` installed on your system for MP3 audio support.
- Python 3.10 recommended (TensorFlow 2.10 compatibility).

